* SID - SYMBOLIC DEBUGGER

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* SID - SYMBOLIC DEBUGGER

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:SID [program [symbols]]

Loads the CP/M symbolic debugger for private program development. The
supplied SID is an 8080-style debugger; use its command set rather than
assuming a Z80 monitor syntax.

Debugger commands can examine/change memory, set breakpoints and execute
loaded code. A typical private session starts with SYSUTLS:SID
I0:TEST.COM. Use copied files and avoid debugging the live caller service.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
